      <p class="eyebrow">About ACBLPE</p>
      <h2 id="about-title">Two decades of Iberian-<br />lexified creole<br />scholarship</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="about-copy">
      <p>
        ACBLPE is a scientific association dedicated to the study of Iberian-lexified
        creole languages and their communities, and more generally linguistic
        contact involving Portuguese or Spanish.
      </p>
      <p>
        Since 2001 its annual meetings have been held in Europe, Africa, the
        Caribbean and South America, alternating where possible between the
        Iberian Peninsula and other parts of the world.
      </p>
      <p>
        The 25th Conference extends this trajectory to South Asia, bringing
        creolists into dialogue with researchers of the Indian Ocean’s
        linguistic and historical contexts.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

